<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns AA to NSW TCorp dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns AA to NSW TCorp dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard and Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Tuesday it had assigned its AA rating to New South Wales Treasury Corp's (TCorp) 15 billion yen 4.8 percent yen/U.S. dollar dual-currency Eurobond due March 13, 2000.</p>
<p>The rating reflects that of its guarantor, the State of New South Wales, S&amp;P said in a statement.</p>
<p>The rating of the bonds is constrained by Australia's foreign currency sovereign rating of AA, it said. The foreign currency rating outlook is positive, S&amp;P said.</p>
</text>
